e confirms or contradicts the premise's exact dependency structure for this artifact's own s1-s6 set.","action":"Re-run the ordering probe scoped only to this artifact's own DEF.md Section 6 (grep 'Depends on:' within that specific file) to directly confirm or refute the s1-s6 chain as stated, instead of relying on a cross-epic, cap-truncated grep that cannot address this artifact's specific claim.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The grounding tool returned generic, unscoped evidence from unrelated epics rather than this artifact's own Section 6 dependency lines, so the premise's specific s1-s6 chain can be neither confirmed nor refuted from what was handed over.","options":["Re-run the probe scoped to this artifact's own file path and confirm the s1-s6 dependency chain directly against its Section 6","Manually inspect this artifact's Section 6 and each story's Depends-on line to verify the claimed chain is acyclic and correctly ordered"]}},{"claimId":"indexed-only-difference-semantic","ref":"k9 / S6.1 ac1","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Per constraint k9 and Story s6 acceptance criterion ac1, indexed review differs from diff-based review only in permitting caller/impact queries for changed methods or entities; every other behavior (scoped commit packets, evidence, continuation, recovery, completion semantics) is asserted to be identical between the two modes.","evidence":"DEF.md:180 (ac1) states verbatim: 'both entrypoints and both grounding modes use the same scoped commit packets, PLAN-directed investigation, evidence, continuation, recovery and completion semantics. Indexed mode differs only in caller lookup and impact analysis; small and planless builds remain supported and no generic HEAD or working-tree diff silently changes scope.' k9 (DEF.md:88) corroborates: 'Indexed review differs only by permitting caller queries for methods/entities changed in the selected commit packets and impact analysis from those results... index results never select additional review commits or silently substitute for authoritative packet/source evidence.' Both anchors independently confirm the premise's claim that the only behavioral delta is caller/impact querying, with all other semantics (scoped commit packets, evidence, continuation, recovery, completion) asserted identical across modes.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":7,"low":5},"reviewedAt":"2026-10-28T06:28:56.348Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
